# text
seg-76cf2fbbdc07 = Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct

# text
seg-159ab7b65b97 = Our Pledge

# text
seg-621b620ca2da = We as members, contributors, and leaders pledge to make participation in our community a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex characteristics, gender identity and expression, level of experience, education, socio-economic status, nationality, personal appearance, race, caste, color, religion, or sexual identity and orientation.

# text
seg-17faa5ea9b6d = We pledge to act and interact in ways that contribute to an open, welcoming, diverse, inclusive, and healthy community.

# text
seg-2731f1ded8ec = Our Standards

# text
seg-5016f4dfccfb = Examples of behavior that contributes to a positive environment for our community include:

# text
seg-bdbcfe06d29f = Demonstrating empathy and kindness toward other people

# text
seg-a1299fe3447b = Being respectful of differing opinions, viewpoints, and experiences

# text
seg-065c753f9c7d = Giving and gracefully accepting constructive feedback

# text
seg-4806be549906 = Accepting responsibility and apologizing to those affected by our mistakes, and learning from the experience

# text
seg-894eeb3ccede = Focusing on what is best not just for us as individuals, but for the overall community

# text
seg-32de193d3520 = Examples of unacceptable behavior include:

# text
seg-05dd86b3f11d = The use of sexualized language or imagery, and sexual attention or advances of any kind

# text
seg-e77cf145fd02 = Trolling, insulting or derogatory comments, and personal or political attacks

# text
seg-3309de60bddb = Public or private harassment

# text
seg-9607974b6b48 = Publishing others' private information, such as a physical or email address, without their explicit permission

# text
seg-4678428c1f03 = Other conduct which could reasonably be considered inappropriate in a professional setting

# text
seg-8e1c53718966 = Enforcement Responsibilities

# text
seg-2de9f6a8a8b3 = Community leaders are responsible for clarifying and enforcing our standards of acceptable behavior and will take appropriate and fair corrective action in response to any behavior that they deem inappropriate, threatening, offensive, or harmful.

# text
seg-75fef1ab1542 = Community leaders have the right and responsibility to remove, edit, or reject comments, commits, code, wiki edits, issues, and other contributions that are not aligned to this Code of Conduct, and will communicate reasons for moderation decisions when appropriate.

# text
seg-08994a4765be = Scope

# text
seg-0a62c85e8cf3 = This Code of Conduct applies within all community spaces, and also applies when an individual is officially representing the community in public spaces. Examples of representing our community include using an official e-mail address, posting via an official social media account, or acting as an appointed representative at an online or offline event.

# text
seg-d387e0c041e6 = Enforcement

# text
seg-54d4988a6315 = Instances of abusive, harassing, or otherwise unacceptable behavior may be reported to the community leaders responsible for enforcement at <a1>contact@ashforde.org</a1>. All complaints will be reviewed and investigated promptly and fairly.

# text
seg-826819c7b6bf = All community leaders are obligated to respect the privacy and security of the reporter of any incident.

# text
seg-5e5a97c9bdc1 = Enforcement Guidelines

# text
seg-09afb39b9789 = Community leaders will follow these Community Impact Guidelines in determining the consequences for any action they deem in violation of this Code of Conduct:

# text
seg-7acf4903ad52 = { "1" }. Correction

# text
seg-ee49590aacdd = <b>Community Impact</b>: Use of inappropriate language or other behavior deemed unprofessional or unwelcome in the community.

# text
seg-6c7e7f8181cf = <b>Consequence</b>: A private, written warning from community leaders, providing clarity around the nature of the violation and an explanation of why the behavior was inappropriate. A public apology may be requested.

# text
seg-db3674eeed2e = { "2" }. Warning

# text
seg-eb9356b85662 = <b>Community Impact</b>: A violation through a single incident or series of actions.

# text
seg-bd1a70f3d25c = <b>Consequence</b>: A warning with consequences for continued behavior. No interaction with the people involved, including unsolicited interaction with those enforcing the Code of Conduct, for a specified period of time. This includes avoiding interactions in community spaces as well as external channels like social media. Violating these terms may lead to a temporary or permanent ban.

# text
seg-9209f93b77ee = { "3" }. Temporary Ban

# text
seg-2ceee18edcb0 = <b>Community Impact</b>: A serious violation of community standards, including sustained inappropriate behavior.

# text
seg-49825371297f = <b>Consequence</b>: A temporary ban from any sort of interaction or public communication with the community for a specified period of time. No public or private interaction with the people involved, including unsolicited interaction with those enforcing the Code of Conduct, is allowed during this period. Violating these terms may lead to a permanent ban.

# text
seg-602026c2d3ed = { "4" }. Permanent Ban

# text
seg-99e67abb8978 = <b>Community Impact</b>: Demonstrating a pattern of violation of community standards, including sustained inappropriate behavior, harassment of an individual, or aggression toward or disparagement of classes of individuals.

# text
seg-809fa976dce8 = <b>Consequence</b>: A permanent ban from any sort of public interaction within the community.

# text
seg-86c668236bcd = Attribution

# text
seg-a61a93ee3757 = This Code of Conduct is adapted from the <a1>Contributor Covenant</a1>, version { "2.1" }, available at <a2>https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct.html</a2>.

# text
seg-6309372ba614 = Community Impact Guidelines were inspired by <a1>Mozilla's code of conduct enforcement ladder</a1>.

# text
seg-1a3df1951a1e = For answers to common questions about this code of conduct, see the FAQ at <a1>https://www.contributor-covenant.org/faq</a1>. Translations are available at <a2>https://www.contributor-covenant.org/translations</a2>.

